<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sasol year shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Sasol year shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 25</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     393.1	 vs 323.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 122.5	 vs 102.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2,333.0     vs 1,859.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3,449.0     vs 2,830.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 924.0	 vs 934.0</p>
<p>    Net interest received 277.0	 vs 144.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  13,545.0    vs 11,955.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast an earnings per share figure for synthetic fuels produce Sasol of 385-400 cents and a dividend of 116.0 to 130 cents a share.  </p>
<p>Full name: Sasol Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
